Use three semaphores: `mutex = 1`, `empty = n`, `full = 0`.

```
Producer:            Consumer:
wait(empty);         wait(full);
wait(mutex);         wait(mutex);
add item             remove item
signal(mutex);       signal(mutex);
signal(full);        signal(empty);
```

The order matters: if the producer did `wait(mutex)` before `wait(empty)` on a full buffer, it would hold the mutex while waiting, the consumer could never enter, and the system would deadlock.

